B.Pt=new A.bn("CTO (Yale or Minerva)",B.ah,"CTO: Yale brace or Minerva body jacket","Unstable lower cervical fractures requiring multi-planar control benefit from CTOs that extend to the thorax for improved lever arm and motion restriction.","Yale brace = Philadelphia collar + thoracic extension. Minerva provides circumferential head/thorax control without halo pins.")
B.Pu=new A.bn("Halo vest",B.ah,"Halo vest","Gold standard for unstable upper cervical spine injuries. Provides the greatest restriction of cervical motion of any orthosis (>95% restriction in all planes).","Halo vest provides the most cervical restriction of any orthosis. Pin torque: 8 in-lb (adults), 2-4 in-lb (children). Watch for pin-site infections.")
B.Pv=new A.bn("C-Leg 4 or Rheo Knee 3",B.ah,"C-Leg 4 or Rheo Knee 3","Both are top-tier microprocessor knees. The Rheo Knee uses magnetorheological fluid and demonstrates 5% less metabolic cost compared to the C-Leg in studies.","Rheo Knee 3 uses magnetorheological (MR) fluid \u2014 5% less metabolic cost vs C-Leg. C-Leg uses hydraulic cylinder with microprocessor control.")
B.Pw=new A.bn("Multi-axis foot",B.ah,"Multi-axis foot","Allows motion in all three planes (sagittal, frontal, transverse), improving accommodation on uneven terrain for limited community ambulators.","Multi-axis feet allow inversion/eversion and transverse rotation \u2014 best for uneven terrain ambulation.")
B.Px=new A.bn("CTO or SOMI",B.ah,"Cervicothoracic orthosis (CTO) or sternal-occipital-mandibular immobilizer (SOMI)","For stable upper cervical fractures, a CTO or SOMI provides adequate immobilization without the complications of halo pin fixation.","SOMI is best for mid-cervical (C2-C5) flexion control (~93% restriction) but does NOT effectively restrict C1-C2 motion and is poor in extension (~42%). CTO provides more balanced multiplanar control.")
B.Py=new A.bn("Philadelphia or Miami J collar",B.ah,"Philadelphia collar or Miami J collar","For stable lower cervical fractures requiring multiplanar control without maximum restriction. These rigid collars restrict approximately 70% of flexion/extension.","Miami J is a modified Philadelphia collar with improved ventilation and adjustability. Both restrict ~70% of overall cervical motion.")
B.QG=new A.bs("Transradial","trEnvironment")
B.QF=new A.bs("Transhumeral","thPriority")
B.Q9=new A.bs("Shoulder+","shoulder")
B.Z4=s([B.QG,B.QF,B.Q9],t.j)
